# State & Data Fetching

## Server state

All API data via TanStack Query. Use configured `queryClient` from `@/shared/services/queryClient`.

## Query keys

- Lists: `['users-list', page, search, sortBy, sortOrder]`
- Detail: `['user', id]`
- Auth: `['auth-user']`
- Settings: `['global-settings']`, `['countries-list', ...]`

## Mutations

- `onSuccess`: invalidate related queries + `toast.success`
- `onError`: map 422 to form or `toast.error(getErrorMessage(error))`
- `retry: 0` for mutations (configured globally)

## Do not

- Create duplicate axios instances
- Use raw `fetch()` for API calls
- Store server data in useState when Query can hold it
